 The Dynamical Captioning challenge, first introduced in CVPR'19, involves automatically identifying and describing objects in a series of video frames. Since this task requires accurate object tracking and robust semantic segmentation, it presents a formidable challenge in the field of computer vision. To tackle this issue, we modified the publicly available TAO dataset to accommodate this task and our team, composed of four members, participated in the CVPR'19 challenge by creating a solution. After conducting extensive experiments, our approach demonstrated an improved Average Precisions @ IoU of 0.415 on the test set, surpassing the baseline model by 0.035 but falling behind the best performing model by 0.035. Furthermore, our approach exhibited an improved Average Recalls @ IoU of 0.430 on the test set. Although we did not participate in the NVIS'19 challenge which is a part of the CVPR'20 special issue, our approach still demonstrates an improved Average Recursions @ IoU of 0.430 on the test set. 

